Default process metrics (CPU, heap, event-loop lag) are already wired via
`collectDefaultMetrics()` in main.ts and served at GET /metrics
(infrastructure/http/controllers/health.controller.ts) using prom-client's
default registry — that's what docker-init/grafana/provisioning/dashboards/
scheduler-overview.json reads from.

This directory is for domain-specific counters/histograms once the scheduler
domain exists (e.g. booking_conflict_total, availability_check_duration_seconds)
— see docs/09_devops_infrastructure.md. Cortex's equivalent directory only
holds outbox.metrics.ts, which is T3-only (no outbox here) and not ported.
